eturn value, and frees the program (matching the C `sloth.c`)\n\n### Verification\nI verified the implementation against the C test suite (`tests.c`):\n1. `parse(\"Examples/HelloWorld.sloth\")` produces the exact expected bytecodes (1, 3, 1, ..., 8 at index 14, 10 at index 17)\n2. `parse(\"Examples/Gamut.sloth\")` covers all 10 instruction opcodes\n3. `execute(parse(\"Examples/Count.sloth\"))` returns `11` (counting from 1 to 10 with newlines)\n\nNo `unsafe`, no FFI, no `unimplemented!`/`todo!`/`panic!` placeholders remain."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":330,"cache_read_input_tokens":46359,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":330,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0eebed29-c1b4-439c-a05c-0ddfcaf22c28","uuid":"f5a1be90-3ff6-459b-9587-f2276466d546"}
